     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is five times the maximum recommended dose, which is 10 mg daily. At that dose it could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and shock. The usual adult starting dose is 2.5 to 5 mg daily.\n\nThe order may be a typo, such as 5 mg written as 50 mg, or the amlodipine dose may have been intended for a different patient. Please check the original prescription with the prescribing physician before anything is entered.\n\nAlso, medication orders need to come from a licensed prescriber. Once the prescriber confirms the dose, they or a clinician on the medicine service should enter the order. If you give me the prescriber's confirmed dose and their credentials, I can help you draft the order for them to review."
      }
